cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this software or its results, cite it as below. Any use beyond reading requires written permission: mrala@ut.ac.ir"
title: "tsp-lab: Beam-Guided Memetic Annealing (BGMA) and LKH, benchmarked"
abstract: >-
  A TSP laboratory in JavaScript. It contains Beam-Guided Memetic Annealing
  (BGMA), an anytime polynomial-time heuristic with a low/mid/high/xhigh/max
  effort ladder; an independent Lin-Kernighan-Helsgaun (LKH) solver; a
  Held-Karp exact solver for n <= 22; a Held-Karp-style 1-tree lower bound; and
  a benchmark suite scoring every method against exact optima, published TSPLIB
  optima and the 1-tree bound. Headline measured results: BGMA returns the
  published optimum on 9/9 TSPLIB instances up to n = 417 at every effort
  level, and deviates by +0.33% to +2.10% at n = 574-1060; the 1-tree bound is
  shown to overstate the true gap by up to 5.34 percentage points.
